⚠️ Security Tips
Review unexpected processes in ps aux.
Check unknown listening ports with ss -tulnp.
Audit SUID binaries regularly.
Use SHA-256 instead of MD5 for integrity checks.
Correlate findings with system logs.
📝 Key Takeaways
ps aux, top, and htop are used for process monitoring.
lsof -i, netstat, and ss analyze network activity.
ls -lah, find, and stat inspect file permissions and metadata.
md5sum and sha256sum verify file integrity.
These commands are foundational for Linux administration and cybersecurity.
📚 One-Line Summary
Linux provides powerful built-in commands to inspect processes, monitor network connections, audit permissions, and verify file integrity—essential skills for system administrators and cybersecurity professionals.
